    title "2020 CTIA 5G Summit | COVID-19: Wireless Keeps Americans Connected"
    description "COVID-19 prompted sudden and significant changes in how we live, work, and educate. Through it all, America&#8217;s wireless networks rose to the occasion, capably handling unprecedented surges in mobile voice and data traffic, facilitated by a national policy that favors investment, innovation and competition. This panel brought together thought leaders across the wireless industry to discuss how the response to COVID-19 demonstrated consumer reliance on wireless, ushered in a new era of telehealth, distance learning and mobile workforces and can lead to policies that enhance consumer access to mobile wireless services.&#10;&#10;Speakers:&#10;&#8226;Grant Spellmeyer, VP, Federal Affairs &#38; Public Policy, U.S. Cellular&#10;&#8226;Michele Thomas, VP, State Government Affairs, T-Mobile&#10;&#8226;David Villyard, Deputy Director, National Communication Coordination, DHS&#10;&#8226;Matthew Gerst, VP, Regulatory Affairs, CTIA&#10;&#10;Watch on-demand videos of all keynotes and panels on the CTIA website: https://ctia.it/34nfZ42"
